printer-soc/services/helixscreen/docs/devel/architecture/06-discovery-capabilities.md:122:One honesty note the older documentation obscures: `SensorRegistry` ([`include/sensor_registry.h#SensorRegistry`](../../../include/sensor_registry.h#L60)) — the "central registry" that fans `discover_all()`/`update_all_from_status()` across managers — is never instantiated in production; its only constructions are its own unit tests ([`tests/unit/test_sensor_registry.cpp`](../../../tests/unit/test_sensor_registry.cpp), 15 of them). The live wiring is direct: `PrinterDiscovery::parse_objects()` calls five managers' `discover()` itself ([`src/printer/printer_discovery.cpp#fsm`](../../../src/printer/printer_discovery.cpp#L105)-131), the discovery sequence's `configfile.config` step queues `ProbeSensorManager` and `AccelSensorManager` `discover_from_config()` to the main thread ([`src/api/moonraker_discovery_sequence.cpp#continue_discovery_objects`](../../../src/api/moonraker_discovery_sequence.cpp#L883)-775 — accel sensors appear *only* there), and status frames fan out to all seven from `PrinterState::update_from_status()` ([`src/printer/printer_state.cpp#update_from_status`](../../../src/printer/printer_state.cpp#L638)-646). The mock seeds the same managers directly ([`src/api/moonraker_client_mock.cpp#populate_capabilities`](../../../src/api/moonraker_client_mock.cpp#L787), `:906`), so `--test` exercises identical code paths.
